From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tu Dinh <ngoc-tu.dinh@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 23:35:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xen/grant-table: Use INIT_DELAYED_WORK_ONSTACK in
 gnttab_unmap_refs_sync

gnttab_unmap_refs_sync may take an in-stack gntab_unmap_queue_data
object. Using INIT_DELAYED_WORK on it is safe since
gnttab_unmap_refs_sync waits for the completion of the entire unmap, but
it may still lead to an "ODEBUG: object is on stack, but NOT annotated"
warning if CONFIG_DEBUG_OBJECTS_WORK is enabled.

Open code the initialization of item->gnttab_work in
gnttab_unmap_refs_sync instead in order to avoid this warning. Add a
matching destroy_delayed_work_on_stack for the work item.

Signed-off-by: Tu Dinh <ngoc-tu.dinh@vates.tech>

diff --git a/drivers/xen/grant-table.c b/drivers/xen/grant-table.c
index e434a583ee7e..9a1a9bcffb6c 100644
--- a/drivers/xen/grant-table.c
+++ b/drivers/xen/grant-table.c
@@ -1158,8 +1158,12 @@ int gnttab_unmap_refs_sync(struct gntab_unmap_queue_data *item)
 	init_completion(&data.completion);
 	item->data = &data;
 	item->done = &unmap_refs_callback;
-	gnttab_unmap_refs_async(item);
+	INIT_DELAYED_WORK_ONSTACK(&item->gnttab_work, gnttab_unmap_work);
+	item->age = 0;
+
+	__gnttab_unmap_refs_async(item);
 	wait_for_completion(&data.completion);
+	destroy_delayed_work_on_stack(&item->gnttab_work);
 
 	return data.result;
 }
